00:06:14.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Bonnie's bed was kept pushed up against one wall, and her pillows lay against this wall instead of beneath Bonnie's head. When police pulled the bed away, they found her pajamas stuffed beneath the pillows between the mattress and the wall. The pajama top was heavily stained with blood. Bonnie's underpants had been cut, with two slashes made by either a knife or scissors extending from the elastic waistband to the bands where each of Bonnie's legs would go. Given the amount of blood on Bonnie's pajama top, it seemed strange there was so little around her actual wound. It appeared that after the killer stabbed Bonnie, they had rolled her over onto her stomach, then removed her pajamas and washed her with water, which soaked the mattress. Faint smearing across Bonnie's torso indicated that her body had been wiped clean. Frank and Mavis Church ushered Marion back to their home to comfort her while the police remained at the Clark resident with Bonnie.

