00:14:16.000 --> 00:15:03.000
The only people who lived in the residence were Marion and Bonnie. Marion said she'd left Bonnie's father, Dennis, due to his alcoholism and occasional violin outbursts. Although this description might have made Dennis sound like a possible suspect, he had a solid alibi for the night of December 20 and was quickly ruled out of the investigation. But there was something about Bonnie's mother that gave Detective Lily pause. Although Bonnie's murder looked to have a sexual component, there was no seaman present, and the assault of Bonnie had been digital. These factors led Detective Lily to suspect that a woman was behind the crime. And the most obvious woman,

