He'd been working at the cinema where he was employed as an assistant projectionist. The police in 1982 had ruled him out and gone back to the drawing board. Detective Tim Day decided to search the Criminal Records branch for any mention of a Mow Clark. He couldn't find anything. The closest he could find was an offender named Joe Clark, who had been convicted of two separate violent crimes committed in the years before and after Bonnie's murder. In June of 1980, Teresa Crow was a 22-year-old who loved to dance. A friendly, outgoing and vivacious young woman, one of her favourite things to do was go to a disco named Chasers in the inner-city Melbourne suburb of Peran. Teresa became a fixture at Chasers, which led to her meeting a wide circle of friends.

